# Grid A — S3 Config trace (effective-value precedence)
#
# Targets: config_trace scenario + ReqConfigMapping + ShapeConfigValue.
# Validates the config resolution chain explanation: code-default →
# codrax.yaml → CLI flag precedence, with DefaultExploreHeuristics
# as the concrete example the user picked.
#
# Ground truth (CLAUDE.md §Configuration + internal/types/config.go):
# explore_* group merges onto types.DefaultExploreHeuristics; only
# bare + pipeline_* groups accept CLI flags, so explore_* is
# YAML-only. Positive anchor requires both the YAML filename and the
# default struct to be named. Negative anchor blocks the generic
# "read from environment variables" hallucination — codrax does not
# use env vars for this group.
ID="s3a"
NAME="config trace — explore_mid_loop_hint_budget precedence"
QUESTION="explore_mid_loop_hint_budget 的最终有效值是怎么计算出来的？给我 code default / codrax.yaml / CLI 三层的覆盖优先级。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC required 2 anchor names
# but didn't gate on the question's CORE answer — that explore_*
# group is YAML-only (no CLI flag). Tighten by requiring the
# answer to (a) state the precedence rule (code default → yaml →
# CLI) AND (b) note that explore_* group lacks CLI binding (the
# load-bearing fact for this question). Generic chain-listing
# without the "no CLI for explore_*" verdict no longer PASSes.
#
# 2026-05-06 vocabulary broadening: real eval surfaced LLMs
# correctly identifying the struct + file:line that holds the
# defaults (ExploreHeuristics at internal/types/config.go:831)
# without literally writing the function name DefaultExploreHeuristics.
# Substantively the struct + line IS where defaults live; the
# Default<X>() function returning that struct is a synonymous
# handle, not the only acceptable identifier. EC now accepts
# "ExploreHeuristics" (the struct), which DefaultExploreHeuristics
# also matches as a substring — both function-naming and
# struct-naming pass. Negative regex still requires the "no CLI
# binding" verdict; broadened to accept 无绑定 / 不绑定 / 不存在
# (no-绑定 vs 未-绑定 was a single-character mismatch the LLM hit).
# 2026-06-13 vocabulary broadening (third, audited): the question's
# key is a DELIBERATE probe — it is shaped like an explore_* knob but
# absent from the config surface by design (the prompt-side identifier
# denylist carries it precisely so prompts can never hardcode it).
# Two substantively-correct answers FAILed on anchor wording alone:
# (a) "在 CLI flag 注册段也无任何绑定" missed the contiguous 无绑定
#     alternation by one inserted word → accept 无(任何)?绑定;
# (b) an answer grounded the family via the real neighbours
#     ExploreMidLoopMinIteration / loop_max_midloop_injects /
#     MaxMidLoopInjects instead of naming the ExploreHeuristics
#     struct → the positive anchor becomes an alternation over REAL
#     same-family identifiers (every alternative exists in code and
#     cannot be produced by echoing the probe key; the camel form of
#     the probe key itself is deliberately NOT accepted).
# Load-bearing assertions are unchanged: precedence chain wording,
# the YAML filename, the no-CLI/no-binding verdict, and the env-var
# negative all still gate.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="codrax.yaml"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(default|默认值|默认值|代码默认)
(yaml|codrax\.yaml)
(ExploreHeuristics|ExploreMidLoopMinIteration|ExploreMidLoopEnumCoverage|explore_midloop_min_iteration|explore_midloop_enum_coverage|MaxMidLoopInjects|loop_max_midloop_injects)
(no CLI|CLI flag.*not|no flag|没有.*CLI|未绑定|无(任何)?绑定|不绑定|不接受|不存在.*CLI|CLI.*不存在)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="os.Getenv environment.variable .env"
